------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Bundled conversion tools
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

medmcp-dicom wraps established third-party DICOM and neuroimaging software, and
the published container image redistributes the dcm2niix binary. Each remains
under its own license and carries its own citation requirements; if you use the
results in research, please cite the underlying methods (see the "Citation"
section of README.md).

  - dcm2niix (convert_dcm_to_nifti, build_bids_dataset) — DICOM to NIfTI
    conversion, invoked as a subprocess.
    BSD-3-Clause, Copyright (c) 2014-2021 Chris Rorden.
    https://github.com/rordenlab/dcm2niix
    Cite: Li et al., "The first step for neuroimaging data analysis: DICOM to
    NIfTI conversion", Journal of Neuroscience Methods 264:47-56 (2016).
    doi:10.1016/j.jneumeth.2016.03.001
    dcm2niix incorporates further components under their own terms — public
    domain (niftilib, miniz), MIT (ujpeg), BSD (OpenJPEG, CharLS), zlib, and
    JasPer — with the per-file breakdown in the license.txt that ships inside
    the distributed package.
    Upstream states that dcm2niix is developed for research purposes only and
    is not a clinical tool, which matches this project's own position.

  - pydicom (explore_dicom, and DICOM header reading throughout) — pure-Python
    DICOM library. MIT. https://github.com/pydicom/pydicom

  - nibabel (inspect_nifti, explore_bids) — read/write access to neuroimaging
    file formats. MIT. https://github.com/nipy/nibabel

No pretrained model weights are bundled or redistributed by this stack.

